-- Help Center: say plainly that the price shown is the price paid (owner decision 2026-11-11: no sales tax added; US dollars) and which payment methods Stripe offers. Appends one line to the four articles that explain paying,
-- only while updated_by is still 'seed' (an article edited in Admin > Help Center is left alone) and only once. Not reviewed by an accountant.
UPDATE help_articles SET body = body || char(10) || char(10) || 'The price you see is the price you pay. We do not add sales tax. Prices are in US dollars. You can pay by card, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Amazon Pay, Cash App Pay or Link. Which options you see depends on your device and location. Optional automatic renewal needs a card.' WHERE slug IN ('contest-passes', 'event-partner-plan', 'feature-an-event-or-home', 'sponsor-your-installer-company') AND updated_by = 'seed' AND instr(body, 'We do not add sales tax.') = 0;
